  [PASS] V1a  this audit reproduces g04's published Sedna MI-A significances   (worst relative deviation from g04's printed 0.005/0.05 (canonical) and 0.010/0.10 (alt) is 6.1%, which is the rounding of the 1-2 significant figures g04 prints.  The integrator, design matrix, weights and projector are lifted verbatim, so the machinery is not in dispute -- only the attribution of the shortfall is)
  [PASS] V2a  the shortfall factorises exactly into instrumental x structural   (worst |INSTR*STRUCT/total - 1| = 2.2e-16.  The decomposition is an identity, not a model: 3/chi_post = (3/chi_raw)(chi_raw/chi_post).  There is no third factor to hide in)
  [FAIL] V3a  THE CLAIM: the shortfall is STRUCTURAL rather than INSTRUMENTAL at the headline precision   (IT IS NOT, at the 100 mas footing that carries the headline 0.005 sigma / 639x.  There the INSTRUMENTAL factor is 32x (canonical) / 15x (alt) and the STRUCTURAL factor is only 20x / 20x.  The signal is 32x too small for 100 mas astrometry BEFORE a single orbital element is fitted; switching the 4-element absorption off entirely still leaves 0.094 sigma, 32x short of 3.  The orbit-fit absorption is the SMALLER of the two effects at the headline precision, so 'structural, NOT instrumental' inverts the actual ranking.  (At 10 mas the ranking does flip -- INSTR 3.2x vs STRUCT 20x -- so the honest statement is that BOTH factors independently suffice at 10 mas and the instrumental one dominates at 100 mas.  The negative itself is untouched: Sedna falls short either way))
  V4 -- MUTATION CONTROL: does the projector discriminate, or does it eat everything?
  omega+1e-9 (IN-family)     chi_raw  4.1304e-02  chi_post  3.7705e-17  absorbed factor   1.095e+15
  dg = 1e-12 (AU/r)^3        chi_raw  1.1232e-06  chi_post  1.1217e-06  absorbed factor   1.001e+00
  dg = 1e-12 const           chi_raw  6.8433e-02  chi_post  3.4144e-03  absorbed factor   2.004e+01
  [PASS] V4a  MUTATION CONTROL: in-family absorbed >1e4x more strongly than out-of-family   (a pure omega shift (which IS one of the 4 fitted elements) is absorbed by a factor 1.1e+15, while the out-of-family radial perturbations are absorbed by only 2.0e+01.  A ratio of 5.5e+13.  So the factor-16 absorption reported for MI-A is a REAL partial degeneracy and not a projector that flattens everything -- g04's structural mechanism is genuine, it is only its RANKING against the instrumental factor that this audit disputes)
  V5 -- 'more telescope does not help, only more decades do' -- quantified at the PRESENT 25-yr arc
  MI-A on the existing 25-yr arc reaches 3 sigma at a per-epoch astrometric precision of 156 micro-arcsec (0.156 mas), at 401 epochs.
  Equivalently, at 10 mas it needs 1.64e+06 epochs -- which is the route that really is shut.
  g04's D4a scan instead extends the ARC and finds 3 sigma at ~400 yr.  Both statements are true; g04
  scans only one axis and then asserts the other axis is closed.  0.156 mas is 64x
  beyond LSST-class but it is not centuries away, and Sedna is V=20.6 -- within reach of a dedicated
  space-astrometry programme in principle.  Reported as a caveat on the framing, not as a live proposal.
  [FAIL] V5a  the precision axis is as closed as the arc axis (needs > 1e6 x better astrometry)   (NOT AT THAT LEVEL.  The required per-epoch precision on the existing arc is 0.156 mas = 156 uas, only 64x beyond the 10 mas LSST-class figure g04 uses -- not the 'centuries, not a bigger telescope' dichotomy D4a asserts.  The epoch count route is genuinely shut (1.6e+06 epochs at 10 mas), and the overall NEGATIVE stands, but the specific claim that only more decades help is not established by the scan D4a actually ran)
  V6 -- is MI-A an envelope over MODIFIED INERTIA, or only over Route A's own kernel?
  Milgrom's theorem (1994, Ann. Phys. 229, 384) fixes MI = MG for CIRCULAR orbits.  Sedna's orbit is
  nowhere near circular and nowhere near deep-MOND: its APHELION sits at y = g_N/a_0 = 72 (canonical),
  sqrt(y) = 8.5, i.e. DEEP NEWTONIAN.  No theorem constrains MI there.  So MI-A/MI-B are not envelopes
  derived from MI; they are Route A's EXPONENTIAL kernel evaluated at the orbit's minimum acceleration.
  But the exponential approach to Newton is a MODIFIED-GRAVITY fit choice.  MI's own kernel is not fixed
  by it -- that is the whole content of the fork.  The standard MOND interpolating families approach
  Newton as a POWER law, nu - 1 ~ 1/y (the 'simple'/RAR family), not as exp(-sqrt y).  On Sedna's
  aphelion that is the difference between 1/(e^8.5-1) = 2.0e-4 and 1/72 = 1.4e-2: a factor ~68.

  MI reading                           dg [m/s2]    / a_0   post mas  sig@100   sig@10
  can MI-A, Route A exp kernel         1.375e-12    0.015  2.263e-02    0.005     0.05
  can MI-A, power-law nu-1 = 1/(2y)    4.680e-11    0.500  7.705e-01    0.160     1.60
  can MI-A, anomaly of order a_0       9.360e-11    1.000  1.541e+00    0.320     3.20
  alt MI-A, Route A exp kernel         2.952e-12    0.026  4.860e-02    0.010     0.10
  alt MI-A, power-law nu-1 = 1/(2y)    5.650e-11    0.500  9.302e-01    0.193     1.93
  alt MI-A, anomaly of order a_0       1.130e-10    1.000  1.860e+00    0.386     3.86

  BUT THE COUNTEREXAMPLE MUST ITSELF SURVIVE THE INNER PLANETS.  Under the SAME MI-A ansatz, Mars's
  anomaly is keyed to MARS's aphelion, so any MI kernel generous at Sedna is also generous at Mars.
  Scan the one-parameter power-law family nu - 1 = y^-p (normalised so nu - 1 = 1 at y = 1, which is
  what galaxy rotation curves require of any MOND-class kernel) and impose EVERY planetary bound:
       p  binding planet  dg(Sedna)/a_0   dg [m/s2]  sigma @10mas
   1.000         Mercury         1.0000   9.360e-11           nan
   1.250         Mercury         0.3430   3.210e-11           nan
   1.500           Earth         0.1176   1.101e-11           nan
   1.656            Mars         0.0603   5.647e-12           nan
   1.750         ALLOWED         0.0403   3.776e-12          0.14
   2.000         ALLOWED         0.0138   1.295e-12          0.05
   2.500         ALLOWED         0.0016   1.523e-13          0.01
   3.000         ALLOWED         0.0002   1.792e-14          0.00
  The planetary bounds force p > ~1.66 (Mars binds); at the boundary the Sedna anomaly is capped at
  0.040 a_0 = 3.78e-12 m/s^2, giving 0.14 sigma at 10 mas on the 25-yr arc.
  [PASS] V6a  MI-A bounds every modified-inertia reading, so 'shut for the most generous is shut for all'   (UPHELD, BUT NOT FOR THE REASON g04 GIVES, AND ITS SCOPE MUST BE NARROWED.  Taken at face value the envelope claim fails: MI-A is the most generous reading of ROUTE A'S EXPONENTIAL kernel, not of modified inertia, and Sedna's aphelion sits at y = 72 -- DEEP NEWTONIAN, where Milgrom's circular-orbit theorem says nothing and MI's interpolating behaviour is not fixed by the MG fit.  A free anomaly of order a_0 along the orbit gives 3.2 sigma (canonical) / 3.9 (alt) at 10 mas, ABOVE 3, so MI-A is NOT an envelope over the class.  What rescues the conclusion is a constraint g04 never invokes here: under the SAME MI-A ansatz the inner planets are bound too, and Mars forces any power-law kernel nu-1 = y^-p (normalised to O(1) at y ~ 1, as rotation curves require) to p > 1.66, capping Sedna at 0.040 a_0 = 0.14 sigma at 10 mas.  So the NEGATIVE survives on the one-parameter power-law family -- by an inner-planet argument, not by MI-A being an envelope.  It is NOT established for kernels with intrinsic eccentricity dependence, which a genuinely nonlocal MI has and which Mars (e = 0.09) cannot constrain from Sedna (e = 0.85))
